Spec: Bounded Android control session

Purpose:
  Negotiate, register pending declarations and query explicit operations through a verified transport port.

Owns:
  ./ControlSession.java

Must:
  Require negotiated pending capability and explicit experimental opt-in before mutation, with no automatic retry/reconnect or generated operation UUID.
  Allow one request at a time, verify peer before and after transport and discard late results after close/timeout/cancel.
  Before transport entry mark a mutation as possibly submitted; map subsequent lost/invalid replies, timeout or close to unknown outcome with its original UUID.
  Preserve standard future cancellation semantics while retaining operation ID and possible-submission metadata on mutation futures.
  Keep valid Broker errors distinguishable from transport uncertainty and return fixed local errors.
  Negotiate secure stream capabilities before optional open, scoped grant and native descriptor operations.
  Serialize descriptor attachment with control exchanges, retain its original open operation and close late native results.

  Require separate relay capability negotiation and experimental opt-in for relay opens; a live relay response without negotiation is rejected, while closed historical outcomes remain queryable.
  Negotiate formal connection capability separately, retain open/attach/close operation IDs and query their typed results without parsing them as registration outcomes.
